WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.383 --> 00:00:18.565
Yog sang out, appearing suddenly in the middle of the sitting room.

2
00:00:19.225 --> 00:00:20.886
Zann spun around, startled.

3
00:00:21.566 --> 00:00:24.968
Over an hour had passed since he and his friends had been locked in the suite.

4
00:00:25.629 --> 00:00:28.390
Darb and the girls were playing with a deck of cards they'd found.

5
00:00:29.011 --> 00:00:31.032
But Zann was too restless to sit still.

6
00:00:31.788 --> 00:00:37.030
He was wandering from window to window, staring out at the palace courtyard while trying to figure out

7
00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:37.590
what to do.

8
00:00:38.631 --> 00:00:42.312
Jumping to her feet, Perda asked Yog,"Did you come to let us out?"

9
00:00:43.093 --> 00:00:43.873
Yog smiled.

10
00:00:43.893 --> 00:00:45.013
"Sorry, no.

11
00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:46.454
I'm here to conjure your dinner."

12
00:00:46.474 --> 00:00:48.095
"Where's Zing?"

13
00:00:48.535 --> 00:00:49.215
Zann demanded.

14
00:00:49.235 --> 00:00:52.236
"Who? Oh, the dragon," Yog said.

15
00:00:52.256 --> 00:00:53.597
"Don't worry, he's fine.

16
00:00:54.377 --> 00:00:58.999
Zing's having a great time hanging out with some cute female vapor bounders in the palace menagerie."

17
00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.120
"You can't keep us here."

18
00:01:01.596 --> 00:01:02.437
Gliss frowned at him.

19
00:01:02.457 --> 00:01:04.178
"It's not right."

20
00:01:05.299 --> 00:01:06.060
Yog sighed.

21
00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.583
"Look, you have to understand it's not safe for you out there.

22
00:01:10.283 --> 00:01:11.364
Especially you two Reds.

23
00:01:11.724 --> 00:01:13.826
There are still trolls all over the city.

24
00:01:14.487 --> 00:01:17.669
You're better off staying here, under the protection of the palace."

25
00:01:17.689 --> 00:01:20.912
"The palace didn't protect the king and queen," Perda pointed out.

26
00:01:21.653 --> 00:01:22.333
Zann nodded.

27
00:01:22.353 --> 00:01:25.916
"We need to figure out what Morb is doing with all those Reds."

28
00:01:26.937 --> 00:01:28.638
"We're working on that," Yog said.

29
00:01:28.658 --> 00:01:30.500
"We have spy flies everywhere."

30
00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:32.641
"So what have you found out?"

31
00:01:32.961 --> 00:01:33.561
Perda asked.

32
00:01:34.242 --> 00:01:36.063
Zann didn't expect Yog to answer.

33
00:01:36.443 --> 00:01:36.923
But he did.

34
00:01:36.943 --> 00:01:39.765
"Morb has changed his method," Yog said.

35
00:01:39.785 --> 00:01:44.347
"When he took the king and queen, he and his trolls zapped away with them immediately."

36
00:01:45.108 --> 00:01:46.088
Gliss looked sad.

37
00:01:46.108 --> 00:01:48.530
"Yeah, that's what happened with my parents."

38
00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:53.652
"The spy flies show that the trolls are still grabbing Reds," Yog went on.

39
00:01:53.672 --> 00:01:57.214
"But now they're holding them prisoner right here in First City."

40
00:01:58.035 --> 00:01:59.195
"Really?" Darb said.

41
00:01:59.215 --> 00:02:03.205
"Where?" "The wild dragon pen at the zoo," Yog replied.

42
00:02:03.226 --> 00:02:06.227
"It's the only natural vacuum within the city limits.

43
00:02:07.128 --> 00:02:12.070
Dangerous dragon species are kept in that pen because dragons aren't able to use their magic in there."

44
00:02:12.991 --> 00:02:13.991
Gliss gasped.

45
00:02:14.011 --> 00:02:17.834
"The trolls are throwing the Reds in with a bunch of wild dragons?

46
00:02:18.794 --> 00:02:22.656
Even if the dragons can't use magic, the bigger ones could still kill someone!"

47
00:02:22.676 --> 00:02:24.777
"The dragons aren't there anymore."

48
00:02:25.518 --> 00:02:27.039
Yog paused, looking worried.

49
00:02:27.059 --> 00:02:29.040
"Nobody's sure what happened to them."

50
00:02:29.956 --> 00:02:34.379
"Why would Morb keep his prisoners in the city instead of zapping them away?"

51
00:02:34.839 --> 00:02:35.419
Zann wondered.

52
00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:37.200
Yog shrugged.

53
00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.261
"Nobody knows.

54
00:02:39.021 --> 00:02:43.584
But Slib is supposed to be figuring out a plan to rescue the prisoners before Morb takes them

55
00:02:43.624 --> 00:02:46.525
away." Zann traded a glance with his friends.

56
00:02:47.205 --> 00:02:49.687
It sounded as if Yog didn't think much of Slib.

57
00:02:49.707 --> 00:02:52.548
"Maybe we can help," Zann said.

58
00:02:52.568 --> 00:02:55.430
"If you let us out—" "Nice try."

59
00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.331
Yog gave him a sympathetic smile.

60
00:02:57.351 --> 00:02:59.132
"Now, what would you like for dinner?"

61
00:03:01.684 --> 00:03:06.528
Yog conjured plenty of food for them, along with pajamas and everything else they asked for.

62
00:03:07.269 --> 00:03:11.132
When Zann and his friends were busy eating, Yog stepped to the center of the room.

63
00:03:11.152 --> 00:03:12.934
"Good night," he said.

64
00:03:12.954 --> 00:03:14.995
"I'll be back in the morning to make you breakfast."

65
00:03:15.756 --> 00:03:18.778
Then he covered his mouth with his hand and whispered something.

66
00:03:19.519 --> 00:03:21.000
A second later he was gone.

67
00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:23.342
"Did anybody hear the password?"

68
00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:24.283
Zann asked.

69
00:03:25.364 --> 00:03:26.225
Darb shook his head.

70
00:03:26.245 --> 00:03:27.626
"I was too far away."

71
00:03:27.646 --> 00:03:29.948
"We all were," Gliss said.

72
00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:32.662
"We would've needed a Swelling spell to hear it."

73
00:03:33.403 --> 00:03:34.944
"Oh well," Perda said.

74
00:03:34.964 --> 00:03:37.866
"Maybe we could try to hear it when he comes back in the morning."

75
00:03:38.607 --> 00:03:41.289
"I wonder why Morb is keeping the prisoners at the zoo."

76
00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:43.391
Gliss took a sip of her drink.

77
00:03:43.731 --> 00:03:46.113
"Why wouldn't he just zap them away like the others?"

78
00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:49.696
"Maybe he left the trolls in charge," Darb suggested.

79
00:03:49.716 --> 00:03:53.319
"Without extra magic they can't zap anyone anywhere."

80
00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:55.121
Zann hadn't thought of that.

81
00:03:55.141 --> 00:03:58.143
"Trolls can't do much magic, can they?"

82
00:03:58.524 --> 00:03:58.864
he said.

83
00:03:59.532 --> 00:04:00.392
Darb shook his head.

84
00:04:00.412 --> 00:04:03.073
"They can't even conjure up enough food for themselves.

85
00:04:03.773 --> 00:04:07.154
That's why they're always causing trouble, raiding villages near their territory.

86
00:04:07.974 --> 00:04:13.636
Morb must be providing extra magic so they can zap themselves long distances and do everything else they've

87
00:04:13.656 --> 00:04:14.396
been doing lately."

88
00:04:14.416 --> 00:04:16.757
"So why did he stop?"

89
00:04:17.157 --> 00:04:17.757
Gliss wondered.

90
00:04:18.397 --> 00:04:19.097
Perda shrugged.

91
00:04:19.117 --> 00:04:21.998
"Maybe kidnapping the king and queen weakened him."

92
00:04:22.698 --> 00:04:25.159
Zann was already losing interest in the conversation.

93
00:04:25.839 --> 00:04:28.600
He didn't want to sit around, talking about Morb's trolls.

94
00:04:29.384 --> 00:04:34.788
As far as Zann was concerned, they needed to find Boz's Magic Master friends as soon as possible.

95
00:04:35.748 --> 00:04:36.689
He pushed away his plate.

96
00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.210
"Who cares why?

97
00:04:39.211 --> 00:04:43.073
Let's get some sleep so we'll be ready to find a way out of here first thing tomorrow."

98
00:04:43.834 --> 00:04:45.395
"Okay," Perda said.

99
00:04:45.415 --> 00:04:46.456
"Come on, Gliss.

100
00:04:47.236 --> 00:04:48.417
We'll take the big bedroom.

101
00:04:48.998 --> 00:04:50.338
The boys can take the other one."

102
00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:58.184
It had been a long, exhausting day, and despite his worries, Zann fell asleep almost immediately.

103
00:04:58.944 --> 00:05:03.647
He wasn't sure how long he'd been asleep when he was startled awake by something brushing against his

104
00:05:03.708 --> 00:05:05.629
face. "Who's there?"

105
00:05:05.969 --> 00:05:08.331
he blurted out, wondering if he was still dreaming.

106
00:05:09.071 --> 00:05:13.094
There was no answer except a soft snore from the direction of Darb's bed.

107
00:05:13.855 --> 00:05:17.637
It was dark in the room, but something pale was fluttering around Zann's head.

108
00:05:18.678 --> 00:05:19.699
It was a message moth!

109
00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.741
Zann sat up quickly, holding out his hand.

110
00:05:23.361 --> 00:05:24.722
The moth landed on his finger.

111
00:05:25.443 --> 00:05:29.010
Zann climbed out of bed, hurried to the window, and pulled back the curtain.

112
00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:32.952
It was almost dawn, and there was just enough light for him to see.

113
00:05:33.993 --> 00:05:35.594
Zann peered at the moth's wings.

114
00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:38.456
To his surprise one of them was blank.

115
00:05:39.097 --> 00:05:41.478
Whoever had sent this moth hadn't signed it.

116
00:05:42.279 --> 00:05:46.702
"That's weird," Zann thought, quickly turning his gaze to the other wing.

117
00:05:47.683 --> 00:05:52.366
Just a few words were scrawled there, and Zann's eyes widened as he read them.

118
00:05:53.066 --> 00:05:55.228
The password is zipflower.
